  "ticket_id": "88d2-6756",
  "items": [
    {
      "original_text": "A CodeQL job is added to .github/workflows/ci.yml that runs on every PR, scans the code, and uploads results to GitHub's code-scanning API.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system capability where CodeQL scanning is continuously performed on every PR as an ongoing workflow behavior"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "A code-quality job (or step) emits SARIF output from existing lint/static-analysis tooling (ruff for Python, actionlint for workflows, shellcheck for bash) and uploads via github/codeql-action/upload-sarif so the Require code quality results rule has data to gate against.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable capability where the CI system continuously emits and uploads SARIF output to enable quality gating, not a one-time migration task"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "provision-ruleset.sh extended with require_codeql (boolean) and require_code_quality (boolean) knobs that toggle those Ruleset rules; defaults to false on new projects.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system capability where the script permanently supports configuration knobs for toggling ruleset rules with specific defaults"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "This project's GitHub Ruleset has Require CodeQL and Require code quality rules enabled (matching the 2026-04-28 manual adjustments) \u2014 verified in-session via gh api repos/.../rulesets.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable configuration state of the GitHub Ruleset that persists after this work, though the verification clause adds slight transitional flavor"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "A deliberate test PR with a known CodeQL-detectable security issue (e.g., insecure deserialization pattern) blocks merge until the issue is fixed \u2014 verified in-session.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a one-time verification task (testing that a PR is blocked) rather than an ongoing system property"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "**SC (self-use, Probe-1 remediation, architecture-vs-evidence audit 2026-05-16):** Before the 88d2 sprint can be marked complete, the new `require_codeql` and `require_code_quality` GitHub Ruleset rules are enabled on the DSO repo, AND at least one sprint PR is gated by the new rules. Verification (in-session): `gh api /repos/$OWNER/$REPO/rulesets | jq '[.[] | select(.rules[]?.type == \"code_scanning\")] | length'` returns \u22651; `gh api /repos/$OWNER/$REPO/pulls/<sprint-pr>/checks --jq '[.check_runs[] | select(.name | test(\"CodeQL|code-quality\"))] | length'` returns \u22651.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "completion of a one-time setup task with specific verification criteria that confirms task done-ness rather than describing ongoing system behavior"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    }
  ]
}
